.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Routines for managing quadrants as elements of trees and subtrees\&. 

In addition, some high level algorithms such as \fBp4est_partition_given\fP\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void p4est_balance_subtree (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_connect_type_t\fP btype, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP which_tree, \fBp4est_init_t\fP init_fn)"

.PP
Balances a sorted tree within a \fBp4est\fP\&. It may have exterior quadrants\&. The completed tree will have only owned quadrants and no overlap\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The \fBp4est\fP to work on\&. 
.br
\fIbtype\fP The balance type (face or corner)\&. 
.br
\fIwhich_tree\fP The 0-based index of the subtree to balance\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p4est_complete_region (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, const \fBp4est_quadrant_t\fP * q1, int include_q1, const \fBp4est_quadrant_t\fP * q2, int include_q2, \fBp4est_tree_t\fP * tree, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP which_tree, \fBp4est_init_t\fP init_fn)"

.PP
Constructs a minimal linear octree between two octants\&. This is algorithm 2 from H\&. Sundar, R\&.S\&. Sampath and G\&. Biros with the additional improvements that we do not require sorting and the runtime is O(N)\&.
.PP
\fBPrecondition\fP
.RS 4
\fIq1\fP < \fIq2\fP in the Morton ordering\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP Used for the memory pools and quadrant init\&. 
.br
\fIq1\fP First input quadrant\&. Data init'ed if included\&. 
.br
\fIinclude_q1\fP Flag to specify whether q1 is included\&. 
.br
\fIq2\fP Second input quadrant\&. Data init'ed if included\&. 
.br
\fIinclude_q2\fP Flag to specify whether q2 is included\&. 
.br
\fItree\fP Initialized tree with zero elements\&. 
.br
\fIwhich_tree\fP The 0-based index of \fItree\fP which is needed for the \fCp4est_quadrant_init_data\fP routine\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p4est_complete_subtree (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP which_tree, \fBp4est_init_t\fP init_fn)"

.PP
Completes a sorted tree within a \fBp4est\fP\&. It may have exterior quadrants\&. The completed tree will have only owned quadrants and no overlap\&. Note that the tree's counters (\fIquadrants_per_level\fP, \fImaxlevel\fP) must be correct for the quadrants in the incoming tree\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The \fBp4est\fP to work on\&. 
.br
\fIwhich_tree\fP The 0-based index of the subtree to complete\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.RE
.PP

