.SS "int p4est_is_valid (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est)"

.PP
Check a forest for validity and allreduce the result\&. Some properties of a valid forest are: the quadrant counters are consistent all trees are complete all non-local trees are empty This function is collective! It is also relatively expensive, so its use in production should be limited\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The forest to be tested\&. Itself and its connectivity must be non-NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns true if valid, false otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "size_t p4est_linearize_tree (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_tree_t\fP * tree)"

.PP
Remove overlaps from a sorted list of quadrants\&. This is algorithm 8 from H\&. Sundar, R\&.S\&. Sampath and G\&. Biros with the additional improvement that it works in-place\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP used for the memory pool and quadrant free\&. 
.br
\fItree\fP A sorted tree to be linearized in-place\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns the number of removed quadrants\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int p4est_next_nonempty_process (int rank, int num_procs, \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP * num_quadrants_in_proc)"

.PP
Find next non-empty process\&. Finds the next process id >= \fIrank\fP which is not empty according to \fInum_quadrants_in_proc\fP\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIrank\fP process id where search starts 
.br
\fInum_procs\fP number of processes 
.br
\fInum_quadrants_in_proc\fP number of quadrants for each process 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
process id of a non empty process 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp4est_locidx_t\fP p4est_partition_correction (\fBp4est_gloidx_t\fP * partition, int num_procs, int rank, \fBp4est_gloidx_t\fP min_quadrant_id, \fBp4est_gloidx_t\fP max_quadrant_id)"

.PP
Compute correction of partition for a process\&. The correction denotes how many quadrants the process with id \fIrank\fP takes from (if correction positive) or gives to (if correction negative) the previous process with id \fIrank-1\fP in order to assign a family of quadrants to one process\&. The process with the highest number of quadrants of a family gets all quadrants belonging to this family from other processes\&. If this applies to several processes, then the process with the lowest id gets the quadrants\&. A process can give more quadrants than it owns, if it passes quadrants from other processes\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpartition\fP first global quadrant index for each process (+1) 
.br
\fInum_procs\fP number of processes 
.br
\fIrank\fP process id for which correction is computed 
.br
\fImin_quadrant_id\fP minimal global quadrant index of family 
.br
\fImax_quadrant_id\fP maximal global quadrant index of family 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
correction for process \fIrank\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp4est_gloidx_t\fP p4est_partition_for_coarsening (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP * num_quadrants_in_proc)"

.PP
Correct partition counters to allow one level of coarsening\&. No quadrants are actually shipped, just the desired number is updated\&. This function guarantees that empty processors remain empty\&. This function is collective and acts as a synchronization point\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP forest whose partition is corrected 
.br
\fInum_quadrants_in_proc\fP partition that will be corrected 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
total absolute number of moved quadrants\&. In practice, at most a small number per processor\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp4est_gloidx_t\fP p4est_partition_given (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, const \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP * num_quadrants_in_proc)"

.PP
Partition \fI\fBp4est\fP\fP given the number of quadrants per proc\&. Given the desired number of quadrants per proc \fInum_quadrants_in_proc\fP the forest \fI\fBp4est\fP\fP is partitioned\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP the forest that is partitioned\&. 
.br
\fInum_quadrants_in_proc\fP an integer array of the number of quadrants desired per processor\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns the global count of shipped quadrants\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBExamples\fP
.in +1c
\fBtimings/timings2\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "unsigned p4est_quadrant_checksum (sc_array_t * quadrants, sc_array_t * checkarray, size_t first_quadrant)"

.PP
Computes a machine-independent checksum of a list of quadrants\&. 
.PP
