.SS "void p4est_tree_compute_overlap (\fBp4est_t\fP * p4est, sc_array_t * in, sc_array_t * out, \fBp4est_connect_type_t\fP balance, sc_array_t * borders, sc_array_t * inseeds)"

.PP
Compute the overlap of a number of insulation layers with a tree\&. Every quadrant out of the insulation layer of the quadrants in \fIin\fP except the quadrant itself is checked for overlap of quadrants from all trees that are smaller by at least two levels and thus can cause a split\&. Those elements that cause a split (as determined by the p4est_balance_*_test routines) create quadrants in \fIout\fP that will reproduce those splits when \fIin\fP is balanced\&. Note: Use this version if you are using less than full balance\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP The \fBp4est\fP to work on\&. 
.br
\fIin\fP A piggy-sorted linear list of quadrants\&. The piggy2->from_tree member must be set\&. 
.br
\fIout\fP A piggy-sorted subset of tree->quadrants\&. 
.br
\fIbalance\fP The type of balance condition that should be enforced\&. 
.br
\fIborders\fP Array of arrays of tree border elements: if not NULL, this will be used to fill \fIout\fP\&. 
.br
\fIinseeds\fP The seeds that \fIin\fP generates locally\&. 
.RE
.PP

